 succeeded in 313ms:
docs/doc-P.md:27:- **f32 meaning:** evaluate the chosen tree literally. Every numeric primitive, including subtraction, `exp`, multiplication and addition in the combine, and every component of `lift`, has the core `fround` meaning. Copies/branches do not do arithmetic; a tag test evaluates only the selected arm. No implicit FMA, reassociation, fast exponential, flush-to-zero or parallel atomic sum. GPU lowering must be checked separately; choosing CUDA `expf` does not prove agreement with `fround(Math.exp(...))`.
docs/doc-P.md:28:- **Law for regrouping:** require a registered real identity and associativity derivation on the reachable, shape-correct states, and closure there. Ordered trees suffice; no commutativity required. This is not an `associative=true` flag about machine floats. Three scalar reductions would be simpler syntax but could not update the two sums from *both* child maxima at a merge. Storing the unnormalized output rather than the running quotient avoids a division at every merge.
docs/doc-P.md:105:2. For **every** tentative intermediate (including new schedules and the final CUDA observation), compare candidate f32 to the same origin f64 under the frozen relation. Use the future Tix evaluators/contract on these ports; do not use the previous approximate result as the oracle. Tolerance is not transitive. Exact local proof does not exempt the whole output from the origin check. A strict/bitwise compilation mode cannot authorize the full chain by these arguments.
docs/doc-P.md:107:The current framework already has the needed *host* interfaces: [directed rewrites and `verify`](../../../../../../src/framework/ir/PATTERNS-AND-REWRITES.md), [`applyPass` with `contractInputs.origin`](../../../../../../src/framework/passes/define-pass.ts), and [`differential`](../../../../../../src/framework/contracts/differential.ts) with baseline/subject execution and a custom comparator. Bind `before`, tentative `after` and immutable `origin` to a versioned transformation contract; verify before publication. Keep rule id/version, substitutions/guard evidence, revisions, chosen tile/tree, contract/evaluator/math-mode versions, case seed/shape, max absolute and budget-normalized error, and first failing `(i,x)` with inputs or regeneration key. Require the entire prescribed case list decided and passed (the generic sampled tally alone can allow some inconclusives). If device math differs from the scheduled f32 evaluator, record the device discrepancy as a lowering difference and check the device output against the origin too; do not classify it as a bit-exact R7 edit. A failed numerical check rejects the candidate, not the real identity. Passing samples is not a universal f32 proof.
docs/doc-P.md:123:## Experiment on NVIDIA GB10
docs/doc-P.md:125:**Hypothesis (pre-register before lowering).** From the literal source, without an attention-named matcher, library dispatch or user annotation, the rule trace produces a checked kernel with no global score/weight buffer. On the six primary shapes `{1024,2048,4096} × {64,128}` (`N,D`), the geometric mean of per-shape derived/unfused **time** ratios will be ≤0.80, derived/hand time ratios ≤1.25, and derived/unfused **DRAM byte** ratios ≤0.75. Report all individual ratios including derived/hand bytes. This tests a performance claim as well as expressibility: a correct but slow fold answers only the latter.
docs/doc-P.md:127:- **Three arms.** Unfused CUDA lowers each original tensor definition separately; materialize `s,e` once, use a competent tiled score producer and parallel independent rows/components, no deliberately repeated dot products. Derived arm takes only the rules above. Independent hand-written, block-streaming CUDA is the positive control. All arms use the same f32 data/layout, precision and math flags (no TF32, half, FMA contraction or fast math), same residency and output, and must pass the origin check. Use the literal score order in all arms; the unfused semantics must retain its source reductions. No precomputed weights. For tiled arms choose legal `R,B` from `{8,16,32} × {16,32,64}` by the same bounded timing budget on separate tuning runs, discard resource-infeasible shapes, then freeze configurations; record launch and resource limits. Give unfused kernels the same tuning opportunity. Every derived tree considered for reporting goes through the gate.
docs/doc-P.md:128:- **Timed quantity.** Measure the whole forward pass on one stream by CUDA events, first launch through final output write, including all unfused kernels. Exclude compile, allocation, migration, host copies and validation. On a dedicated GB10 pre-touch resident buffers, warm each arm 20 times, interleave arms in seeded randomized order over 50 measurement rounds per shape. Use identical cache preparation for all arms (cycle distinct resident input sets totaling more than L2); report median time, dispersion and paired bootstrap 95% intervals for ratios. Record clocks/power mode, driver/toolkit, compiler flags, tile sizes, register/shared usage and spills. Include untimed small/tail cases so a fast full-tile-only kernel cannot pass.
docs/doc-P.md:129:- **Byte quantity.** In separate profiling runs with the same workload/cache policy, query GB10-supported device DRAM read/write byte counters, record their actual names/units, sum both across *all* forward kernels per invocation, repeat five times and take the median. Do not substitute requested load bytes, allocated bytes or theoretical tensor sizes for this metric. Record peak global workspace and inspect allocations/launch trace separately for any `N×N` intermediates. If counters are unavailable, the traffic claim is unmeasured.
docs/doc-P.md:130:- **Interpretation.** Arithmetic remains `Θ(N²D)`. The compulsory input/output footprint is `Θ(ND)` and the derived schedule eliminates the `Θ(N²)` global score/weight writes and their reads. On-chip footprint per query tile is `O((R+B)D + RB)` words including local scores and state. There is **not** a general `O(ND)` bound on measured DRAM traffic on a fixed GB10: absent cache reuse, `ceil(N/R)` query tiles can each reread `Θ(ND)` key/value words. Cache hits, spills and math throughput decide how much of the potential gain appears as bytes or time. Keeping all scores in a single on-chip row is a simpler two-pass scheme for small `N`, but its scratch grows with `N`; it is not this fixed-tile hypothesis.
docs/doc-P.md:131:- **Decision.** Refute the derivation claim on this study if the source needs a special attention rewrite, any required check fails, or global score/weight storage survives. Refute the stated performance target if any measured geometric-mean ratio exceeds its threshold; publish intervals and flag a threshold crossing within the interval as statistically uncertain. Missing GB10 evidence is inconclusive, not a speedup. As an ablation, disable R5 or R6: the remaining dependence on `M` should prevent this one-pass trace. A surviving one-pass result needs its own explanation.
docs/doc-P.md:136:- Implement the fold/rule verifiers and CUDA realization, then collect the pre-registered GB10 evidence; no kernel or measurement is delivered here.
docs/doc-G.md:150:The worktree already has `rewrite`, `applyOnce` and a transactional per-edit `verify` hook. Use that hook with the immediate predecessor, the proposed revision and a fixed origin captured for the entire sequence. Bind the original artifact as the differential baseline and the candidate as the subject. The existing `differential` API supplies side-specific `run`, custom `compare`, seeded cases and counterexamples. Keep the corpus identical across revisions. Require every planned case to be decided for this experiment. Inspect counts because the generic checker can accept a mixture of agreements and inconclusive cases. Save the first failing row/column, seed or explicit input, source f32, reference f64, candidate value, tolerance and revision. Use the existing conformance example as the model for preparing an edit before publication. The small domain-specific addition is a verifier for these six templates and their binders/guards, alongside the ordered-fold node and its evaluator. A generic symbolic algebra engine is unnecessary. [Directed rewrites](../../../../../../src/framework/ir/rewrites.ts) · [Edit acceptance example](../../../../../../src/conformance/03-strategy-contracts.ts) · [Differential checker](../../../../../../src/framework/contracts/differential.ts)
docs/doc-G.md:164:## GB10 experiment and decision
docs/doc-G.md:166:**Hypothesis.** The six rules will derive the loop from the submitted source, without a function-name match or a hand-selected attention kernel. On a GB10, for each primary shape `(N,D)=(1024,64),(2048,64),(4096,64)`, the derived kernel will pass the above checks, use no global score/weight matrix, take at most **80% of unfused time** and at most **125% of hand-written streaming time**, and move fewer measured DRAM bytes than the unfused program. All thresholds are fixed before measurement.
docs/doc-G.md:168:1. Compile the **unfused** source with all five named stages materialized as written. Compile the **derived** artifact by lowering only its explicit maps, folds and tile-local values. Run an independently **hand-written** tiled streaming CUDA kernel with the same score grouping, types and output layout. Save the automatic rule trace and lowered buffer shapes. Check that there is no global `[N,N]` scratch, including equivalently sized flattened allocations. An opaque dispatch to the hand-written kernel would not test derivation.
docs/doc-G.md:169:2. Use identical resident dense row-major f32 inputs, compiler/toolchain, GPU and math settings for all three. Preserve separate multiplies and adds, gradual underflow, division and square-root precision. Disable fast math, contraction, TF32 and mixed precision. Check actual GPU outputs against the origin too, since CUDA elementary functions can differ from JavaScript even at the same type. Permit comparable launch/block tuning on separate calibration inputs. Record query/key tile sizes, per-lane reduction trees, register/shared memory use, spills, compiler flags, driver and device. Any arithmetic regrouping chosen for lowering has to be represented and checked as a new candidate. Keep the increasing-`d` score accumulation for this experiment.
docs/doc-G.md:170:3. Measure median **GPU elapsed time** in milliseconds via events spanning the entire sequence from first kernel to last, per variant and shape. Preallocate buffers and exclude compilation, allocation and host transfers. Warm up each variant with 10 calls, then time 50 calls each in interleaved, seeded order on the same stream. Report medians, interquartile ranges and ratios. Use the same input sequence and cache protocol across variants. Measure bytes separately with a GB10-supported profiler's DRAM read and write byte counters, summed over all launches for one invocation under matched cache conditions. Record actual counter names, units and profiler replay/cache policy. Report read and write counts separately, their sum, and peak global temporary bytes. Allocation sizes and modeled loads are not measurements of DRAM traffic.
