docs/doc-L.md:26:The experiment (Section 9) is run on the GB10: the rule-derived kernel against the literal unfused lowering and a hand-written streaming kernel, measured wall-clock time and DRAM bytes moved, with pre-registered refutation thresholds, plus per-step contract results and measured tolerance headroom as evidence for the derivation claim itself.
docs/doc-L.md:53:- immutable artifacts with content-hash revisions (`src/framework/core/data.ts`);
docs/doc-L.md:54:- versioned definitions: IR kinds, properties, analyses, invariants, transformations with `requires`/`ensures` and cache policy (`src/framework/contracts/README.md`);
docs/doc-L.md:55:- the **sampled differential invariant** (`src/framework/contracts/differential.ts`): generate cases deterministically from a seed, run a baseline and a subject, compare with an exact or approximate `compare`, record agreement/disagreement/inconclusive counts and the first counterexamples;
docs/doc-L.md:58:This design uses exactly that machinery. Each rewrite rule is a transformation whose `requires` is a syntactic pattern analysis (a property on the before-artifact), whose `ensures` is a differential invariant relating before and after, and whose algebraic argument over the reals is a recorded part of the rule's registration — a human proof stated as a lemma, not a machine-checked one, with the machine's guarantees being the side conditions and the per-application differential check. Where a rule additionally needs an algebraic property of a user-supplied function (R5 needs associativity of the combine), that property is registered with the strongest evidence the framework supports: a dedicated versioned checker recognizing the proved family (`proof`-backed), with sampled evidence as the documented weaker fallback.
docs/doc-L.md:62:The Tix front end (parser, typed AST, extent inference), the f32 evaluator with the given meaning, and a meaning contract with a tolerance relation are being built in parallel and are not in this worktree. This design additionally *requires* of that work: an **f64 evaluator** (the same programs, same operation order, every operation computed in IEEE double and unrounded at f32) to serve as the reference. A CUDA path for Tix programs (statement-per-kernel lowering, and a lowering of the Section 4 construct) does not exist yet; building it is the follow-on implementation ticket (Section 11), and the experiment in Section 9 depends on it. Everything in Sections 3–8 is checkable with the host evaluators alone.
docs/doc-L.md:139:- with `twopass`, the emit is a member of the registered rescaling family (first component an arbitrary `S`, second component the literal `1.0`, remaining components arbitrary — see R6).
docs/doc-L.md:224:**Pattern.** A pair statement produced by R3 (mechanically: a state reduction whose combine is the registered two-component rescaling combine) with body `S`, and a statement
docs/doc-L.md:246:**Side conditions.** `B` divides the extent of `j` (no empty blocks; this also keeps the `−∞ ⊕ −∞` case out of the combine); the combine's `Associative` and `Identity` properties are established (Section 7.6: `proof`-backed for the registered rescaling family by the Corollary; sampled evidence otherwise, recorded as such).
docs/doc-L.md:252:**Pattern.** A `blocked(B)` state reduction of the registered rescaling family — mechanically: `emit = (S, 1.0, V₁, …, V_q)` (the shape the PAIR/PAYLOAD rules produce).
docs/doc-L.md:334:Each rule is a framework transformation: `requires` = the syntactic pattern analysis (a versioned analysis over the before-artifact, returning the match bindings); `ensures` = a sampled differential invariant in the style of `src/framework/contracts/differential.ts`, with the before-program as baseline, the after-program as subject, and the rule's relation. Per rule:
docs/doc-L.md:371:**Error model behind the tolerance** (why these numbers): `o` is a convex combination of the `v` rows (weights `e/ℓ ≥ 0` summing to 1 over ℝ), so there is no cancellation amplification. Each accumulated term picks up one rounding per combining operation; the derived form performs per row about `3N` state operations plus the length-`D` inner sums, giving a relative bound of roughly `(3N + 2D + 4)·u` with `u = 2⁻²⁴` — at `N = 1024, D = 256` about `2.2·10⁻⁴`, i.e. ≥ 4× headroom under `τ_rel = 2⁻¹⁰ ≈ 9.8·10⁻⁴`. The no-regression clause holds because the streaming form adds only the rescale multiplications (≈ a factor ≤ 2–3 in op count over the same terms, well inside the same budget). **This model is itself a falsifiable sub-hypothesis (H1b in Section 9): the experiment measures the actual maximum deviation and the headroom; measured headroom below 2× refutes the model**, and the rule versions and domain must then be re-registered with corrected tolerances.
docs/doc-L.md:385:The host f32 meaning is `Math.fround`-based; a CUDA kernel's `expf` (≈ 2 ulp) and default FMA contraction produce different f32 values. The design therefore keeps two relations: the derivation chain is checked on the host evaluator with the relations of 7.1, and the *final kernel* is additionally checked on the GB10 against the same f64 references with a device tolerance `τ_device,rel = 2⁻⁹`, justified by adding the expf and FMA terms to the model. The checked performance build disables FMA contraction (`--fmad=false`) so that the checked binary and the reported binary differ only in flags; both are checked, and the flag choice is recorded with the measurements.
docs/doc-L.md:389:R5 requires `Associative(combine)` (and `Identity(init)`). For the registered rescaling family (the combines of R3/R4, any arity of payload components), the Corollary of Section 5 is the proof; it is registered as a dedicated versioned checker that recognizes the family syntactically, giving `proof`-backed assurance on the combine's provenance. A user-supplied combine outside the family can be evidence-checked by sampled f64 associativity over generated states — that is `checked` assurance, not proof; the design admits it (acceptance of the R5 application then rests entirely on the differential tolerance check, and the evidence record says so), but the attention derivation uses only the proof-backed family. This split mirrors the framework's declared/checked/proof model exactly.
docs/doc-L.md:412:### 9.1 Hypotheses (pre-registered, falsifiable)
docs/doc-L.md:415:- **H1b (error model).** Measured maximum deviation of every rewritten program from the f64 reference is at most half the tolerance (`headroom ≥ 2×`) on every case. **Refuted** by any case with headroom < 2×; consequence: re-derive the model, re-register rule versions.
docs/doc-L.md:426:- **Device**: NVIDIA GB10 (Grace Blackwell, CUDA-capable), CUDA C++.
docs/doc-L.md:427:- **Kernels**: (a) *unfused* — the literal statement-per-kernel lowering of P0 (five kernels: `s`, `m`, `e`, `l`, `o`), tiled matmuls, intermediates in global memory; (b) *hand-written* — an FA2-style f32 streaming kernel written directly in CUDA; (c) *derived* — the lowering of P6 (one CTA per row-tile, sequential over j-blocks, state in registers, K/V blocks staged through shared memory), implementing the P6 schedule exactly, FMA contraction disabled in the checked build (Section 7.5).
docs/doc-L.md:432:- **Time**: CUDA-event wall clock, median of ≥ 100 runs after 20 warmup runs, per shape and block size.
docs/doc-L.md:443:Not a tuning shortfall but a structural failure: no sequence of the stated rules connects P0 to a streaming form on the real program (a side condition that does not hold — e.g. the Tix scoping of `o`'s divisor defeated R1); or a rule that is real-exact but whose f32 deviation escapes the pre-registered tolerance on the accepted domain (H1/H1b); or a derived kernel that nevertheless materializes N² traffic (H3). Any of these convicts a specific named rule or the error model — that is what makes the design falsifiable rather than merely evaluative.
docs/doc-L.md:460:4. **Lowering** — CUDA lowering of the construct (P6 schedule) and the unfused statement-per-kernel lowering of P0.
docs/doc-L.md:461:5. **GB10 rig** — timing, Nsight counters, on-device checks; the H1–H5 verdicts.
docs/doc-L.md:479:FlashAttention (Dao et al., arXiv:2205.14135) and FlashAttention-2 (arXiv:2307.08691) define the target algorithm; the online-softmax rescaling identity and its use for memory-efficient normalization appear in Milakov & Gimelshein (arXiv:1805.02867). The (max, weight-sum) rescaling combine is the soft-max monoid known from the MapReduce/aggregation literature; this design's Lemma 1 is its associativity proof, and its payload extension (Lemma 2) is what attention needs. Chan, Golub & LeVeque's parallel-variance combine is the analogous associativity for R9's future Welford extension. On the compilation side, Taco (arXiv:1612.05201) compiles index notation with workspaces and fusion but not streaming reassociation with checked meaning; Halide and TVM/TensorIR separate meaning from schedule but check schedules by testing, not by per-rewrite meaning contracts; equality saturation (egg, arXiv:1802.10523) is the search-layer alternative discussed in Section 10; Exocompilation proves schedules against semantics but is expert-programmed per kernel. The delta claimed here is narrow and precise: the streaming form reached by directed, individually checked rewrites, each with a pre-registered exact or tolerance relation against the original program's meaning, in a framework whose evidence model distinguishes proof from sample.
docs/doc-A.md:4:The decisive rewrite is to change the reference maximum of a **partial weighted sum**. Once its reference travels with the sum, two disjoint sets of keys can be merged using only their summaries. The score can be any pure scalar expression. The compiler need never match the function name, a dot product, or a CUDA kernel. The claim to test is whether this local derivation preserves the chosen numerical observation and produces competitive code on GB10.
docs/doc-A.md:16:A plan is an ordered binary tree over the increasing indices of J, each present once. A sequential fold starts at id, combines the accumulator with each lifted element, and returns id on an empty range. A block plan folds contiguous nonempty intervals and folds their results in block order, with a short final interval. In reals a registered proof of identity and associativity on reachable summaries licenses the regrouping. Merely supplying a binary expression does not license it. In f32 the tree is part of the program. Evaluate children, then the stated combine expression, rounding literals, shape values, scalar operations and function results exactly as in core Tix, component by component. Tag tests perform no numeric operations. Carry a nonempty child through an empty merge unchanged. No implicit fused multiply-add, reassociation or approximate exponential. A different tree is another checked revision. A scalar-only reduction would require disconnected passes for a maximum and quantities depending on it. An order-only scan would express the sequential recurrence but give no law for combining block results.
docs/doc-A.md:80:The existing pass API accepts a versioned pass, correspondence, declared writes, a transformation contract and extra contract inputs (supply origin = r0). Use an invariant over input and candidate for certificate replay, and differential() with origin and candidate ports, side-specific evaluators, seeded cases and elementwise compare for numerical evidence. Each failing case should identify rule, seed, shape, tree, row/component, expected and actual value. Require every prescribed case to finish; differential() ordinarily allows some inconclusive cases, so count these as suite failures. The framework supplies these hooks. Tix evaluators and a Tix adapter for the extended IR are prerequisites for executing the design.
docs/doc-A.md:82:Use fixed seeds 21, 22, 23 for bounded random inputs at small shapes, plus named cases N=1, D=1, equal scores, tied maxima across blocks, a new maximum in each block, an early dominant score, large negative shifts and alternating signed values. Exercise N=B−1, B, B+1 for B=16,32, and B=1. For example, D=2, q=(8,8) and alternating keys (8,8), (−8,−8) give a shift below −104. Mutate one merge to omit a rescale and one partition to drop the last partial block. The certificate must reject both; require numerical counterexamples on rows with distinct v. Replay numerical checks on actual device output before timing. Compare CUDA with the evaluated plan as well as r0 to distinguish lowering drift from rewrite drift; retain compiler math settings with the result.
docs/doc-A.md:94:## GB10 experiment and decision
docs/doc-A.md:98:On one GB10 use N=256,1024,2048,4096 crossed with D=32,64,128. Preallocate device buffers, warm each configuration for ten calls and collect 50 interleaved, synchronized device-event samples per shape for full forward execution including all unfused kernel launches. Exclude compilation, transfers and allocation from timing. Record software versions, math flags, tile sizes, timing median and interquartile range. Collect device DRAM read plus write bytes across the same kernels in separate counter runs under a documented repeatable cache policy, and record peak live temporary global bytes from allocations. Time is the primary metric; bytes explain whether the intended reduction in traffic occurred.
docs/doc-A.md:108:- Lower the explicit plan to CUDA and run the three-way GB10 experiment when a backend is available.
docs/doc-N.md:86:Use **differential()** as a second invariant, with **origin** as baseline and **output** as subject. Provide the original f64 evaluator, the candidate f32 evaluator and the tolerance comparison above through the existing callbacks. A recorded case succeeds only when its observation was evaluated and met the relation. Use a fixed versioned case suite and report the rule and revisions, matched indices, shape, seed and first failing element with expected, actual and error. Compare every candidate with the original because adjacent tolerance comparisons can accumulate error. The **applyPass** publication gate already supports these contract ports. A single contract on the final fusion would lose the step that introduced a bad match or excess error. No generic framework change is needed for the two invariants. The smallest Tix-specific additions are the ordered fold and an evaluator for its region expressions and state. [Pass integration](../../../../../../src/framework/passes/define-pass.ts), [sampled invariant](../../../../../../src/framework/contracts/differential.ts), [Typed origin example](../../../../../../src/typed/evaluate.ts).
docs/doc-N.md:103:## GB10 experiment
docs/doc-N.md:105:**Hypothesis.** From the given Tix source, the four rules will derive and accept a CUDA-streamable form whose generated kernel meets the fixed numerical gate on the trial suite. For **(N,D) = (4096,64)** and **(8192,64)** on the GB10, its median GPU time will be at most **0.75×** that of the unfused lowering and at most **1.25×** that of an independently written streaming kernel. Its measured DRAM bytes per invocation will be below the unfused lowering's at each primary shape. Predeclare these criteria, the input seeds and the timing protocol.
docs/doc-N.md:107:- Compare the original unfused lowering with separate materialized score and exponential tensors, the derived lowering from the accepted R4 revision, and independently written streaming CUDA. Use row-major inputs, f32 throughout, and the score expression as parsed. For the derived kernel, start with one thread block per eight query rows and 32 keys per tile. Keep q and the running state local to the thread block, share each K/V tile across its rows, and reuse scratch across tiles. Preserve each ordered reduction in the derived IR. Match the baseline and hand kernel on input layout, precision policy and tolerance. The hand kernel can choose its own thread layout and tiling. Require separate multiply and add, gradual underflow and no fast-math modes for the trial. Device exponentiation may differ from rounding the JS double result, so run the same f64 observation check on device outputs. Record the compiler configuration and check the generated artifact for the declared operation and memory policy.
