docs/doc-P.md:2:# From dense softmax to a checked block fold
docs/doc-P.md:4:**Claim to test.** A compiler need not recognize “attention”. It can recognize a sum of weighted values expressed relative to a maximum. Change the reference maximum of one block, and *one scalar* converts the whole block's sum back to the old scale. That fact makes a block replaceable by a fixed-size summary. The dot product is just a producer of scores; the value vector is just one choice of payload.
docs/doc-P.md:8:## Starting point: what the source actually reduces
docs/doc-P.md:22:## Just enough IR: a typed fold with a specified tree
docs/doc-P.md:30:## Rewrite catalogue
docs/doc-P.md:34:**R1 — Substitute a pure tensor definition.** In `A[u]=E; … A[f(j)] …`, substitute `E[u:=f(j)]` at the use. Conversely share identical subexpressions with a scoped `let`. Freshen bound indices, preserve inferred extents as explicit bounds before inlining, check dominance, in-bounds affine substitution, same bindings and exact expression trees. Drop the old definition only with no remaining uses, including the return. SSA lookup and evaluation of the same expression at the same indices give the same value over the reals and bit-for-bit in f32. Check use-def edges, substitution and absence of dangling uses; do not duplicate effects or unroll an unrelated reduction. This rule exposes `t` and `w`, not a promise to recompute a score at each use.
docs/doc-P.md:36:**R2 — Extract a reduction-invariant divisor.** `sum_J (a_j / h) → (sum_J a_j) / h`. Also match a per-term product `(p_j / h) * v_j` as `(p_j * v_j) / h` as part of the same rule. `h` must not depend on `j`; check free indices, type/broadcast and a nonzero finite `h` (here the attained-maximum argument). The real proof is distributivity with constant `1/h`. For an exact-f32-only contract this is not a legal general rewrite: previously each term divided and rounded; now one larger sum rounds before a single divide. With equal logits and values `[1,1,-0.25]`, the two f32 results are `0.5833333730697632` and `0.5833333134651184`. Check the real template **and** tolerance; do not apply to the score just because that divisor is invariant too.
docs/doc-P.md:38:**R3 — Zip independent sums into a product fold.** `(sum_J a_j, sum_J b_j) → fold_J((a_j,b_j), componentwise +, zeros; left)`, including a statically shaped family of sums over `x`. Match identical ordered `J`, independent bodies (neither reads the other's accumulator), compatible row and lane bindings, and exactly the old component seeds and arithmetic. Projection commutes with initialization and every update; induction on the prefix proves equality, bit-exact also in f32. In particular `(w_j,w_j*V_j)` is `w_j P_j` for `P_j=(1,V_j)`; multiplying a finite weight by 1 is exact. A missing unit lane would lose the normalizer. Check by projecting each component back to the old fold.
docs/doc-P.md:40:**R4 — Partition a fold.** For a real monoid `(⊕,id)`, replace a fold on `J` by an outer fold of inner folds with the same operator on `J_b = [bB,min((b+1)B,N))`, `0 ≤ b < ceil(N/B)`, `B` a positive integer. Choose and record the trees; here use increasing left fold across blocks, and ordered midpoint trees for tile max and tile sum. Check integer disjoint, exhaustive, order-preserving coverage (the last block ends at `N`), lift unchanged, units and associativity. Removing units and flattening parentheses gives exactly the original leaf word. For `max` adjoin the core `−∞` empty seed to the finite reals (no subtraction from that seed); for sums use componentwise real addition. A partial block has *no* padding scores. Max alone is exact on these inputs with core max semantics; tiled sums change f32 grouping and need tolerance. Changing a tile width or reduction tree is another checked choice, not permission to reorder silently.
docs/doc-P.md:42:**R5 — Rebase a weighted block sum.** For nonempty `I`, `c=max_I t_j` and invariant finite anchor `a`, rewrite
docs/doc-P.md:50:**R6 — Fold summaries at a common anchor.** Recognize a maximum `A=max_b c_b` and an additive payload `Y=sum_b r(c_b,A) C_b`, with `r(u,v)=exp(u-v)`. Rewrite the pair `(A,Y)` to the following fold of block leaves `Some(c_b,C_b)`:
docs/doc-P.md:62:**R7 — Realize a fold at its consumer.** Replace `fold_left_b(map(summary,b))` by a loop with a private accumulator initialized to `id`; form one block leaf and combine it immediately. Place a shared pure producer in tile-local storage if all its uses there have the same index/value and it is dead at tile exit. Map disjoint rows to a query tile; no new reduction across rows. Check a bijection of block/lane indices, exact inner trees, one writer per output, initialized state, tile capacity and last use before scratch reuse (including required synchronization). After `k` iterations the state *is* the fold of the first `k` leaves by the defining recurrence. Storage placement only changes lifetime. This is an exact real and bit-exact f32 scheduling rule in the IR if the backend realizes those primitives and trees. A loop that computes the right answer but writes every leaf to global memory does not meet the schedule requirement.
docs/doc-P.md:64:## Derivation on the given program
docs/doc-P.md:96:## Acceptance: what counts as a checked step
docs/doc-P.md:98:**Study domain.** Single head, dense, integer `1 ≤ N ≤ 4096`, `1 ≤ D ≤ 128`, matched shapes as in the source. Finite f32 `|q|,|k| ≤ 4`, `|v| ≤ 1` componentwise, including signed zeros and subnormals. These are explicit specialization preconditions to be supplied and checked by the study harness, not properties inferred from tensor types. Finite inputs alone do not prevent an overflowing product or division by zero. Products have magnitude at most 16; even the loose bound `16D` on unscaled partial sums leaves a large overflow margin. Stable exponents have nonpositive arguments, local normalizers include a 1, and payloads are bounded sums on at most 4096 leaves. Underflow of negligible terms is allowed; overflow and NaN are not expected. The empty *state* is needed for the fold seed, not an invitation to normalize an empty row.
docs/doc-P.md:100:**Observation and relation.** Observe only the returned tensor (shape, f32 type, all elements), not temporary weights or a norm averaged over rows. Exact local steps require bit equality to their predecessor including signed zero. For numerical acceptance evaluate the **unchanged Tix source** in f64, preserving scopes, seeds, index order and operator placement, widening the exact same f32 inputs and omitting f32 roundings. Keep its output in f64. This is a numerical oracle, not the reals. Proposed frozen study budget, per element: `abs(got-ref) ≤ 2e-4 + 4e-4 * abs(ref)`; compare in f64, require shape/type as specified and finite observations, treat the two zero signs equally for tolerance. The absolute term matters for signed, nearly cancelling values. These numbers are a hypothesis for this domain, not a bound inferred from testing. Test the original f32 evaluator against this same budget first, and log direct deviations from original f32 at each step too. No tuning the budget after seeing failures.
docs/doc-P.md:102:**Two gates per candidate revision:**
docs/doc-P.md:109:**Challenge set.** Fix seeds `21,22,23` before running. For each seed exercise small full outputs on `N=1,2,3,31,32,33,63,64,65,127` and `D=1,7,64,128` with bounded uniform inputs, and on every timed shape. Include hand-constructed equal/near-tied scores, strictly increasing maxima across tiles, the largest score first vs last, alternating-sign values with nearly zero output, tiny/subnormal inputs, and opposite high scores (e.g. all `q=4`, `k=±4`, `D=128`, where a shifted exponential can round to zero). Try `B=1`, a full row on small cases, and tails. Known negatives: overlapping tiles, dropped tail, using `l` in place of a vector lane, missing `α` in either update, accidental reassociation of the score, or a dependent denominator. Require guard/certificate rejection for invalid edits; run arithmetic mutants in the harness to verify the differential suite detects output-changing mistakes. Persist counterexamples; do not report only aggregate agreement.
