docs/doc-P.md:123:## Experiment on NVIDIA GB10
docs/doc-P.md:125:**Hypothesis (pre-register before lowering).** From the literal source, without an attention-named matcher, library dispatch or user annotation, the rule trace produces a checked kernel with no global score/weight buffer. On the six primary shapes `{1024,2048,4096} × {64,128}` (`N,D`), the geometric mean of per-shape derived/unfused **time** ratios will be ≤0.80, derived/hand time ratios ≤1.25, and derived/unfused **DRAM byte** ratios ≤0.75. Report all individual ratios including derived/hand bytes. This tests a performance claim as well as expressibility: a correct but slow fold answers only the latter.
